(print "")
(begin-tx "LPAD-N4 - the bound underneath both CUSTOM redemption entrypoints")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== LPAD-N4 · 01 · both sides of SPARK|C>X_REEDEM's amount bound ====
(print "--- [LPAD-N4 · 01 · the bound] ---")
;;THE BOUNDARY BETWEEN "ALL" AND "FEW", stated as the two ways it can be crossed. Both custom
;;entrypoints funnel into `SPARK|C>X_REEDEM`, whose enforce is
;;`(and (> redemption-quantity 0.0) (<= redemption-quantity supply))`:
;;  - ALL can only ever fail the LEFT half, because it passes the balance itself as the quantity,
;;    so on the emptied account LPAD-N3 left behind the quantity is 0.0;
;;  - FEW can only ever fail the RIGHT half, because the quantity comes from the caller and can be
;;    driven above the balance. Neither entrypoint can reach the other's half.
;;(The spelling "Redemmption" is the source's; matched verbatim on purpose.)
;;
;;Own transaction ending in (rollback-tx): Rule 9 of REPL_TEST_ARCHITECTURE.md -- an
;;expect-failure on a state-mutating op never shares a committing transaction.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-DPTF:module{DemiourgosPactTrueFungibleV2} DPTF)
        (ref-SPARK:module{SparksV2} DEMIPAD-SPARK)
        (spark-id:string "SPARK-98c486052a51")
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<LPAD-N4>> precondition: LPAD-N3 really did empty the liquid balance"
                0.0 (ref-DPTF::UR_AccountSupply spark-id KST.ANHD))
            (expect-failure "<<LPAD-N4>> CustomRedemAll on an already-empty balance hits the `> 0.0` half"
                "Invalid Redemmption Amount"
                (ref-SPARK::C_CustomRedemAllSparks KST.ANHD KST.EMMA KST.ANHD 0.1))
            (expect-failure "<<LPAD-N4>> CustomRedemFew above the balance hits the `<= supply` half"
                "Invalid Redemmption Amount"
                (ref-SPARK::C_CustomRedemFewSparks KST.ANHD KST.EMMA KST.ANHD 1000000.0 0.1))
        ]
    )
    ""
)
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
;;|| NEXT                   >
;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
(print "")
(begin-tx "LPAD-N5 - SNAKES A_UpdateSharePrice cannot reach DEMIPAD: the caller policy it needs is never held")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== LPAD-N5 · 01 · the share-price updater is refused before it writes ====
(print "--- [LPAD-N5 · 01 · share price] ---")
;;DEFECT FOUND BY THIS BLOCK, AND FIXED 2026-09-14. The diagnosis below is kept verbatim because
;;the MECHANISM is the whole lesson; the assertions are now the positive test it predicted.
;;
;;`DEMIPAD-SNAKES::A_UpdateSharePrice` is reached by nothing in the suite, and the reason is that
;;it cannot be reached by anything AT ALL -- not merely by this fixture:
;;
;;  - it forwards to the sovereign `DEMIPAD::A_DefinePrice`, whose first statement is `P|UEV_IMC`,
;;    an inter-module-caller gate: `U|G::UEV_Any` over DEMIPAD's registered policy guards;
;;  - the guard that would admit SNAKES is `(create-capability-guard (P|SNAKES|CALLER))`, which
;;    SNAKES itself registers into that list in its own `P|A_Define`;
;;  - a capability guard only passes while its capability is IN SCOPE, and `A_UpdateSharePrice`
;;    has no `with-capability` at all. Its sibling `C_Acquire` does the opposite: it wraps
;;    `SNAKES|ACQUIRE`, which composes `P|SNAKES|CALLER`, which is exactly why the deposit it
;;    forwards to passes the same gate.
;;  - and there is no wrapper anywhere else to supply that context: `TS02-CPAD` exposes
;;    `SNAKES|C_Acquire` only, and no module calls `A_UpdateSharePrice`.
;;
;;So the admin guard `GOV|DEMIPAD_ADMIN` underneath is never even consulted, and the requested
;;"non-admin signer is refused" test is not writable: an admin and a non-admin are refused
;;identically, one gate earlier, with the same message. What is pinned instead is the true
;;behaviour -- refused, and NOTHING written. The second assertion is the one that matters: it
;;proves the refusal happens before the update lands, not after a partial write.
;;
;;THE FIX APPLIED: wrapping the body in
;;`(with-capability (P|SECURE-CALLER) ...)` (or any cap composing `P|SNAKES|CALLER`) makes the
;;call succeed, this expect-failure fail, and the block should then be rewritten as the positive
;;test: new price stored, non-admin signer refused by `GOV|DEMIPAD_ADMIN`.
;;
;;Signed as the launchpad admin exactly as `[5.3]` signs its `A_DefinePrice` calls, so the refusal
;;cannot be blamed on a missing signature.
;;Own transaction ending in (rollback-tx): Rule 9 -- an expect-failure on a state-mutating op
;;never shares a committing transaction.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_LPAD", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-SNAKES:module{SaleSnakesV2} DEMIPAD-SNAKES)
    )
    (let
        (
            (before:decimal (ref-SNAKES::UR_DollarSharePrice))
        )
        (map print
            [
                (format "<<LPAD-N5>> share price on record = {}" [before])
                ;;THE REGRESSION. Before the fix this call could not succeed for ANY signer.
                (expect "<<LPAD-N5>> the admin's update is accepted now that P|UEV_IMC can pass"
                    true (> (length (ref-SNAKES::A_UpdateSharePrice 17.5)) 0))
                (expect "<<LPAD-N5>> ...and the new share price is what the reader returns"
                    17.5 (ref-SNAKES::UR_DollarSharePrice))
                ;;non-vacuity: 17.5 must not have been the price already, or the line above proves nothing
                (expect "<<LPAD-N5>> ...which is a real change: 17.5 was not the price before"
                    false (= before 17.5))
            ]
        )
        ;;THE SECOND HALF, and it was NOT WRITABLE before the fix. While P|UEV_IMC refused every
        ;;caller, an admin and a non-admin were rejected identically one gate earlier with the same
        ;;message -- so "the admin gate works" could not be tested at all. Now that P|UEV_IMC passes,
        ;;GOV|DEMIPAD_ADMIN is the gate that decides, and it can be shown to decide.
        (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
        (map print
            [
                (expect-failure "<<LPAD-N5>> a NON-admin is refused -- by the ADMIN gate, now reachable"
                    "Keyset failure"
                    (ref-SNAKES::A_UpdateSharePrice 99.0))
                ;;total refusal, not a partial write: the admin's 17.5 still stands
                (expect "<<LPAD-N5>> ...and the price the admin set is untouched by the attempt"
                    17.5 (ref-SNAKES::UR_DollarSharePrice))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)

;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
;;|| NEXT                   >
;;||>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
(print "")
(begin-tx "LPAD-N6 - CUSTODIANS A_UpdateQuintessencePrice is the same defect in the twin module")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== LPAD-N6 · 01 · the quintessence-price updater is refused before it writes ====
(print "--- [LPAD-N6 · 01 · quintessence price] ---")
;;DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED -- the identical shape to <<LPAD-N5>>, in the twin module.
;;`DEMIPAD-CUSTODIANS::A_UpdateQuintessencePrice` forwards to `DEMIPAD::A_DefinePrice` with no
;;`with-capability`, so `P|SNAKES|CALLER`'s counterpart `P|CUSTODIANS|CALLER` is never in scope
;;and DEMIPAD's `P|UEV_IMC` refuses it. Pinned separately rather than folded into N5 because the
;;two are independent modules: fixing one leaves the other broken, and a single shared assertion
;;would go quiet about the half that was not fixed.
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_LPAD", "caps": [] }])
(let
    (
        (ref-CUSTODIANS:module{SaleCustodiansV2} DEMIPAD-CUSTODIANS)
    )
    (let
        (
            (before:decimal (ref-CUSTODIANS::UR_QuitessencePrice))
        )
        (map print
            [
                (format "<<LPAD-N6>> quintessence price on record = {}" [before])
                ;;THE REGRESSION, twin of <<LPAD-N5>>.
                (expect "<<LPAD-N6>> the admin's update is accepted now that P|UEV_IMC can pass"
                    true (> (length (ref-CUSTODIANS::A_UpdateQuintessencePrice 2.75)) 0))
                (expect "<<LPAD-N6>> ...and the new quintessence price is what the reader returns"
                    2.75 (ref-CUSTODIANS::UR_QuitessencePrice))
                (expect "<<LPAD-N6>> ...which is a real change: 2.75 was not the price before"
                    false (= before 2.75))
            ]
        )
        (env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] }])
        (map print
            [
                (expect-failure "<<LPAD-N6>> a NON-admin is refused -- by the ADMIN gate, now reachable"
                    "Keyset failure"
                    (ref-CUSTODIANS::A_UpdateQuintessencePrice 99.0))
                (expect "<<LPAD-N6>> ...and the price the admin set is untouched by the attempt"
                    2.75 (ref-CUSTODIANS::UR_QuitessencePrice))
            ]
        )
    )
    ""
)
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(env-sigs [])
(rollback-tx)
